--- !u!1001 &1611285841
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 86142730}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 315254417069531506, guid: afb1615dd3b243a449003594175d971a, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: '

        Interaction SDK is a library of modular, composable components
        that allows developers to implement a range of robust, standardized interactions
        (including grab, poke, raycast, and more) for controllers and hands. Interaction
        SDK also includes tooling to help developers build their own hand poses.


        Interaction
        SDK components can be found under the [SDK] Oculus Interaction directory.
        You can find Sample scenes under [SDK] Oculus Interaction / Samples.


        To
        get started with hands on the Interaction SDK, see how to Set Up Hand Tracking.
        Make sure that Hand Tracking Support in the OculusProjectConfig is set to
        Controllers and Hands or Hands Only.

'
